---
// Hammond About page body (pilot). Rendered inside src/pages/about.astro.
---
        <div class="space-y-6 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal/90">
          <p>
            Hammond's history wasn't made in boardrooms. It was made down the highway at the Cave Tangi in Ponchatoula on a Friday night, 
            at Strawberry Stadium on a Saturday afternoon, in the hallways of Hammond High when "Tornadoes" 
            meant something you felt in your chest.
          </p>

          <p>
            These designs come from photographs, postcards, yearbooks — the things that survived when the 
            buildings didn't. Every piece tells a story that somebody who was there will recognize immediately, 
            and everybody else should know.
          </p>

          <p>
            This is Hammond. Not the Hammond of master plans and economic development committees. The Hammond 
            that drove down to dance at the Cave Tangi, cheered at Strawberry Stadium, and sent postcards that said 
            "Greetings from Hammond" in letters six feet tall.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Greetings Postcard Image -->
        <a 
          href="/products/greetings-from-hammond-11x14" 
          class="block mt-16 mx-auto max-w-[70%] transition-transform duration-300 hover:scale-[1.02]"
        >
          <img 
            src="/images/greetings_web.png" 
            alt="Greetings from Hammond vintage postcard design" 
            class="w-full h-auto rounded-sm shadow-[0_4px_12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.15)] border border-light-gray/30"
          />
        </a>
